OL,3,CProgramme listings for TUE 19 MAY
OL,4,G1600FComposer of the Week: Palestrina
OL,5,     GAs young Palestrina makes a name
OL,6,     Gfor himself in Rome, Donald
OL,7,     GMacleod opens the venerable score
OL,8,     Gof the Mass which is considered
OL,9,     Gto have marked a turning point in
OL,10,     Gmusic history.
OL,11,G1700FIn Tune
OL,12,     GLive music from cellist Ariana
OL,13,     GKashefi and pianist Petr Limonov.
OL,14,     GMadison Leonard and Oleksiy
OL,15,     GPalchykov on starring in La
OL,16,     Gtraviata.
OL,17,G1900FClassical Mixtape
OL,18,     GTake time out with a 30-minute
OL,19,     Gsoundscape of classical music,
OL,20,     Gincluding Britten's Cuckoo! for
OL,21,     Gchildren's voices and Purcell
OL,22,     Gsung by Iestyn Davies.
